            {
                "entry_id": "9c70343f-b470-3d83-8650-b3d52a221275",
                "word": "caret",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "8c64b310-7ff5-4739-9157-dbc80adde2e7",
                        "entry_id": "9c70343f-b470-3d83-8650-b3d52a221275",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "carets"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "065977f9-849e-3897-b132-59f0e25dfc1b",
                        "entry_id": "9c70343f-b470-3d83-8650-b3d52a221275",
                        "glosses": [
                            "spool, reel"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "masculine"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c7e39c7d-7a70-481a-bdbb-e540fd50d972",
                                "sense_id": "065977f9-849e-3897-b132-59f0e25dfc1b",
                                "text": "La pêcheur ligne sa ligne quand il la tire de l'eau et l'enroule sur le caret, dévidoir contenant normalement cinquante brasses (90 m) de ligne.",
                                "translation": "The angler lines his line when he pulls it from the water and wraps it around the spool, a reel normally containing fifty fathoms (90 m) of line.",
                                "english": "The angler lines his line when he pulls it from the water and wraps it around the spool, a reel normally containing fifty fathoms (90 m) of line."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "772751eb-2e42-41b8-ba62-57e884f7f91b",
                                "sense_id": "065977f9-849e-3897-b132-59f0e25dfc1b",
                                "text": "Le caret, sur lequel était enroulé la ligne, était attaché au bateau afin d'éviter qu'il ne tombe à l'eau.",
                                "translation": "The spool, around which the line was wound, was attached to the boat to avoid it falling into the water.",
                                "english": "The spool, around which the line was wound, was attached to the boat to avoid it falling into the water."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "783c5def-7b4f-45f9-91c7-f6651e05f520",
                                "sense_id": "065977f9-849e-3897-b132-59f0e25dfc1b",
                                "text": "Le fil obtenu était enroulé sur les carets.",
                                "translation": "The thread obtained was wound around the spools.",
                                "english": "The thread obtained was wound around the spools."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "627b1ce4-e249-3146-ae0d-3614020bd4c1",
                        "entry_id": "9c70343f-b470-3d83-8650-b3d52a221275",
                        "glosses": [
                            "yarn (thread of a rope)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "masculine"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e7424275-900a-4747-a663-d69c1a5a0447",
                                "sense_id": "627b1ce4-e249-3146-ae0d-3614020bd4c1",
                                "text": "Les cordes qui concourent à la formation d'un câble commun, prisés isolément, sont plus solides que le cable lui-meme, dans la proportion d'environ quatre à trois; on a trouvé qu'une corde travaillée avec des carets de cent quatre-vingts à cent trente-cinq verges de longueur, était plus solide que celle provenant de carets réduits à une dimension de cent vingt verges, dans la rapport de six à cinq.",
                                "translation": "The ropes that contribute to a common cable, taken in isolation, are sturdier than the cable itself, in the ratio of about four to three; we have found that a rope worked of yarns of one-hundred-and-eighty to one-hundred-and-thirty-five yards in length, was sturdier than that made of threads reduced to a dimension of one-hundred-and-twenty yards, in the ratio of six to five.",
                                "english": "The ropes that contribute to a common cable, taken in isolation, are sturdier than the cable itself, in the ratio of about four to three; we have found that a rope worked of yarns of one-hundred-and-eighty to one-hundred-and-thirty-five yards in length, was sturdier than that made of threads reduced to a dimension of one-hundred-and-twenty yards, in the ratio of six to five."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b105d134-40ee-4b13-b95b-66cf03dec119",
                                "sense_id": "627b1ce4-e249-3146-ae0d-3614020bd4c1",
                                "text": "Si, au contraire, l'ouvrier, tout en empêchant le toupin de tourner, l'éloigne de l'émerillon, la partie des carets comprise entre l'émerillon et le toupin devient moins tendue et les deux carets vont pouvoir se tordre l'un sur l'autre.",
                                "translation": "If, on the other hand, the worker while preventing the top from turning removes it from the swivel, the part of the yarns between the swivel and the top becomes less taut and the two yarns can be twisted one over the other.",
                                "english": "If, on the other hand, the worker while preventing the top from turning removes it from the swivel, the part of the yarns between the swivel and the top becomes less taut and the two yarns can be twisted one over the other."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f50b617b-433a-4668-a453-1bb6add74aeb",
                                "sense_id": "627b1ce4-e249-3146-ae0d-3614020bd4c1",
                                "text": "Les carets devant produire un toron sont fixés par une de leurs extrémités au crochet de l'émerillon; l'autre extrémité de chacun d'eux est fixée à une molette pouvant lui transmettre par sa rotation un mouvement de torsion.",
                                "translation": "The yarns, ahead of producing a strand of rope, are fixed by one of their ends to a hook on the swivel; the other end of each one is fixed to a wheel which can apply a twisting movement by its rotation.",
                                "english": "The yarns, ahead of producing a strand of rope, are fixed by one of their ends to a hook on the swivel; the other end of each one is fixed to a wheel which can apply a twisting movement by its rotation."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
